  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Make the variable in the brackets the subject of the formula. In this question all variables only take positive values.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x+y=z$ $(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=z-x$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=z\\\\y&=z-x\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$A=\\pi rs$ $(r)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\dfrac{A}{\\pi s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\pi rs\\\\r&=\\frac{A}{\\pi s}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$ax=y^2t$ $(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{ax}{t}}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}ax&=y^2t\\\\y^2&=\\frac{ax}{t}\\\\y&=\\sqrt{\\frac{ax}{t}}\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive square root because all variables are positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$w=\\dfrac12mv^2$ $(v)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$v=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{2w}{m}}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}w&=\\frac12mv^2\\\\2w&=mv^2\\\\v^2&=\\frac{2w}{m}\\\\v&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2w}{m}}\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive square root.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$2\\sqrt{x}=m$ $(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{m^2}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sqrt{x}&=m\\\\\\sqrt{x}&=\\frac m2\\\\x&=\\frac{m^2}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$k=\\sqrt{4mt}$ $(m)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=\\dfrac{k^2}{4t}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}k&=\\sqrt{4mt}\\\\k^2&=4mt\\\\m&=\\frac{k^2}{4t}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$ap=b^2-bp$ $(p)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=\\dfrac{b^2}{a+b}$\n\nCollect the terms containing $p$, then factor out $p$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}ap&=b^2-bp\\\\ap+bp&=b^2\\\\p(a+b)&=b^2\\\\p&=\\frac{b^2}{a+b}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x=\\dfrac{1+t}{1-t}$ $(t)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=\\dfrac{x-1}{x+1}$\n\nClear the denominator, collect the terms containing $t$, then factor.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{1+t}{1-t}\\\\x(1-t)&=1+t\\\\x-xt&=1+t\\\\x-1&=xt+t\\\\x-1&=t(x+1)\\\\t&=\\frac{x-1}{x+1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$c^2=a^2+b^2$ $(a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\sqrt{c^2-b^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}c^2&=a^2+b^2\\\\a^2&=c^2-b^2\\\\a&=\\sqrt{c^2-b^2}\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive square root.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$v=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{n-q}{r}}$ $(r)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\dfrac{n-q}{v^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}v&=\\sqrt{\\frac{n-q}{r}}\\\\v^2&=\\frac{n-q}{r}\\\\rv^2&=n-q\\\\r&=\\frac{n-q}{v^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$v=\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{n-q}{r}}$ $(q)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$q=n-v^3r$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}v&=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{n-q}{r}}\\\\v^3&=\\frac{n-q}{r}\\\\rv^3&=n-q\\\\q&=n-rv^3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$t=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\dfrac{L}{g}}$ $(L)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$L=g\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}t&=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac Lg}\\\\\\frac{t}{2\\pi}&=\\sqrt{\\frac Lg}\\\\\\left(\\frac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2&=\\frac Lg\\\\L&=g\\left(\\frac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$t=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\dfrac{h-k}{g}}$ $(k)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=h-g\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}t&=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{h-k}{g}}\\\\\\frac{t}{2\\pi}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{h-k}{g}}\\\\\\left(\\frac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2&=\\frac{h-k}{g}\\\\g\\left(\\frac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2&=h-k\\\\k&=h-g\\left(\\frac{t}{2\\pi}\\right)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1a+\\dfrac1b+\\dfrac1c=\\dfrac1m$ $(a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\dfrac{mbc}{bc-mc-mb}$\n\nIsolate $\\frac{1}{a}$, use a common denominator, then take reciprocals.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1a+\\frac1b+\\frac1c&=\\frac1m\\\\\\frac1a&=\\frac1m-\\frac1b-\\frac1c\\\\\\frac1a&=\\frac{bc-mc-mb}{mbc}\\\\a&=\\frac{mbc}{bc-mc-mb}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-o",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "o",
        "prompt": "$(A-B)^2+C^2=A^2$ $(A)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=\\dfrac{B^2+C^2}{2B}$\n\nExpand the square; the $A^2$ terms cancel.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(A-B)^2+C^2&=A^2\\\\A^2-2AB+B^2+C^2&=A^2\\\\-2AB+B^2+C^2&=0\\\\2AB&=B^2+C^2\\\\A&=\\frac{B^2+C^2}{2B}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-p",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "p",
        "prompt": "$v=c\\left(\\dfrac1r-\\dfrac1s\\right)$ $(s)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s=\\dfrac{rc}{c-rv}$\n\nIsolate $\\frac{1}{s}$, use a common denominator, then take reciprocals.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}v&=c\\left(\\frac1r-\\frac1s\\right)\\\\\\frac vc&=\\frac1r-\\frac1s\\\\\\frac1s&=\\frac1r-\\frac vc\\\\\\frac1s&=\\frac{c-rv}{rc}\\\\s&=\\frac{rc}{c-rv}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
